  "id": "BIT-tomcat-2026-76183",
  "summary": "Apache Tomcat: Bypass of security constraints for WebSocket endpoints",
  "details": "Authentication Bypass by Alternate Name vulnerability in Apache Tomcat allowed the security constraints for any WebSocket endpoint to be bypassed.\n\n\n\nThis issue affects Apache Tomcat: from 11.0.0 through 11.0.25, from 10.1.0 through 10.1.59, from 9.0.0 through 9.0.121.\n\n\n\nThe following versions were EOS at the time the CVE was created but are \nknown to be affected: from 8.5.0 through 8.5.100, from 7.0.43 through 7.0.109. Other unsupported versions may also be affected.\n\n\n\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 11.0.26, 10.1.60 or 9.0.122, which fix the issue.",
